[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992806415","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-3992806415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":3992806415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t_WQP","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T18:22:15Z","updated_at":"2026-03-26T01:44:10Z","body":"As I mentioned before, since the cost per frame doesn't change, I assume re-hashing is the right direction.\r\n\r\nLooking at the current implementation in this PR, checking collision is performed every single time the track path changes. This means that assuming no collisions occur, adding 1000 tracks results in ~1000!~ `Σ[n=1->999]n` iterations in single frame.\r\n\r\n> My implementation is not exactly what @TokageItLab proposed (with deferred calls and all) because I didn't understand how to do that 😆.\r\n\r\nWhat I recommend is implementing a dirty flag and performing the rehash iteration only once within the `call_deferred()` and `AnimationMixer::_animation_set_cache_update()` functions.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid Animation::_track_update_hash(int p_track) {\r\n\tconst NodePath &track_path = tracks[p_track]->path;\r\n\tconst TrackType track_cache_type = get_cache_type(tracks[p_track]->type);\r\n\ttracks[p_track]->thash = HashMapHasherDefault::hash(Pair<const NodePath &, TrackType>(track_path, track_cache_type));\r\n\t_make_dirty();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid Animation::_make_dirty() {\r\n\tif (dirty) {\r\n\t\treturn;\r\n\t}\r\n\tdirty = true;\r\n\tcallable_mp(this, &Animation::ensure_hashes).call_deferred();\r\n}\r\n\r\nvoid Animation::ensure_hashes() {\r\n\tif (!dirty) {\r\n\t\treturn; // Avoid duplicated call between call_deferred and _animation_set_cache_update.\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\twhile () {\r\n\t\t// Process re-hashing to avoid collision.\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tdirty = false;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid AnimationMixer::_animation_set_cache_update() {\r\n\t// Relatively fast function to update all animations.\r\n\tanimation_set_update_pass++;\r\n\tbool clear_cache_needed = false;\r\n\r\n\t// Update changed and add otherwise.\r\n\tfor (const AnimationLibraryData &lib : animation_libraries) {\r\n\t\tfor (const KeyValue<StringName, Ref<Animation>> &K : lib.library->animations) {\r\n\t\t\tStringName key = lib.name == StringName() ? K.key : StringName(String(lib.name) + \"/\" + String(K.key));\r\n\t\t\tif (!animation_set.has(key)) {\r\n\t\t\t\tAnimationData ad;\r\n\t\t\t\tK.value.ensure_hashes();\r\n\t\t\t\tad.animation = K.value;\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992806415/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992950566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-3992950566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":3992950566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7t_5cm","user":{"login":"ugursoy","id":15056545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU2NTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15056545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy","html_url":"https://github.com/ugursoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T18:53:26Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T02:31:09Z","body":"> Looking at the current implementation in this PR, checking collision is performed every single time the track path changes. This means that assuming no collisions occur, adding 1000 tracks results in 1000! iterations in single frame.\r\n\r\nOh, you include the hashmap lookup cost too. ~~I understand.~~\r\nEdit: though it is n(n+1)/2​ iterations, so 1000 x 999 x 0.5\r\nEdit2: I don't understand. Hashmap lookup should take O(1) right? It is not a vector. Each track only updates once right after track path is set, so adding 1000 tracks would make 1000 iterations -> 1000 x O(1). What am I missing?\r\n\r\n> What I recommend is implementing a dirty flag and performing the rehash iteration only once within the `call_deferred()` and `AnimationMixer::_animation_set_cache_update()` functions.\r\n\r\nAllright makes sense, I'll see what I can do and update this. Thanks.\r\nEdit3: I'm working on this, found some edge cases while working on that so it should take some while.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3992950566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3995947991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-3995947991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":3995947991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7uLVPX","user":{"login":"ugursoy","id":15056545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU2NTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15056545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy","html_url":"https://github.com/ugursoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T08:11:21Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T08:11:21Z","body":"I think this covers the case. Can you check @TokageItLab ?\r\n\r\nThe old PR had some other issues as well. This fixes all the problems I could find and think of. Let me know if there are more.\r\n\r\nTested with the same mrp, still same fps as the master branch.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3995947991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4000093998","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-4000093998","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":4000093998,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ubJcu","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T20:29:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T20:33:08Z","body":"BTW TypeHash is never created outside of the animation, so it actually only needs to be unique, meaning it doesn't even have to be a hash as long as collision avoidance is triggered every time after track path is modified. So an inclemented uint64_t could probably be used instead.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4000093998/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4002953356","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-4002953356","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":4002953356,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7umDiM","user":{"login":"ugursoy","id":15056545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU2NTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15056545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy","html_url":"https://github.com/ugursoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-05T07:38:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-05T07:38:16Z","body":"Using unique IDs instead of hash made this much more human readable and manageable.\r\n\r\nI made a measurement for `ensure_unique_ids` method both for hash version and this version. There is a slight improvement too (1.3ms vs. 1.24ms for 1000 tracks).\r\n\r\n> So an inclemented uint64_t could probably be used instead.\r\n\r\nI kept the ID as `uint32_t` because there will be more than enough space and it is faster to compare.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4002953356/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4015633567","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-4015633567","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":4015633567,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vWbSf","user":{"login":"ugursoy","id":15056545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU2NTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15056545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy","html_url":"https://github.com/ugursoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ugursoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-07T05:29:12Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T05:29:12Z","body":"Updated. FPS is still the same as master.\r\n\r\nI added a Hack of my own. If you think it is not safe, I can undo it.\r\nTo lessen the overhead the following line creates:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntracks[p_track]->path_with_cache_type = StringName(String(p_path) + itos(get_cache_type(tracks[p_track]->type)));\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere, instead of adding the cache type as a string, we can directly add it to the address like so.\r\n```\r\nTypeTrackId get_unique_id() const {\r\n    return (TypeTrackId)(path_with_cache_type.data_unique_pointer()) + get_cache_type(type);\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis should be safe. `StringName::data_unique_pointer()` is of type `_Data`, an internal struct with sizeof 40. So each address will have to span at least 40 bytes of space, meaning range (address, address + 40) will be free from any other `StringName` ptr. Since `TrackCache` value range is up to 8, this can be exploited as an offset. \r\n\r\nCreating the original `StringName` takes 1.75ms for 1000 tracks. This gives a small performance boost and track creation time becomes 1.55ms on average (it was 1.24ms when IDs were used so I think it is a good boost).\r\n\r\n> - If those animations are loaded again, `path_with_cache_type` may end up with a different `data_unique_pointer()`.\r\n\r\nI skipped storing the address value and am directly returning the pointer from the `StringName`. So as long as the `StringName` is created, it should be fine I think.\r\n\r\nFinally I should ask, Since we are letting `StringName` handle the collisions, does deferred call make sense at this point? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4015633567/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017055423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-4017055423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":4017055423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7vb2a_","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-07T18:15:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T18:17:28Z","body":"I think that deferred calls are no longer necessary in the current code.\r\n\r\n> This should be safe. StringName::data_unique_pointer() is of type _Data, an internal struct with sizeof 40. So each address will have to span at least 40 bytes of space, meaning range (address, address + 40) will be free from any other StringName ptr. Since TrackCache value range is up to 8, this can be exploited as an offset.\r\n\r\nHowever, that hack could break if `cache_type` increases in the future, so I think the explanetion of the hack should either be commented, or we should abandon the hack at the cost of some performance.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4017055423/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4049522581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117030#issuecomment-4049522581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117030","id":4049522581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7xXs-V","user":{"login":"ugursoy","id":15056545,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDU2NTQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15056545?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url